What the hell happened here? ==================================================================
What the hell happened here? analyser.memeasm - the analyser of the self-hosted MemeAssembly compiler
What the hell happened here? It does what src/frontend/analyser/{parameters,mod,helper}.rs of the reference do (one input file, -S output, noob mode):
What the hell happened here?   1. classifies every used parameter: TYPE, VALUE, VERBATIM and ESCAPE of the command records (DESIGN.md)
What the hell happened here?   2. rejects pointers that are no register, bad parameter combinations and what x86-64 cannot encode
What the hell happened here?   3. checks the labels: function names, upgrade/banana, monke, who would win (with and without edition), same picture
What the hell happened here?   4. makes the random choices: CONFUSED_INDEX and the commands that "perfectly balanced" deletes
What the hell happened here? Every error calls libFail. There is no main-function check and no call-target check (the reference
What the hell happened here? only does those for executables).
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Monke label prefix of this file: uau. Edition / function prefix: ana.
What the hell happened here? Monke labels are uau + 4 letters for the function + 4 letters for the place in the function.
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Private globals of the analyser (G = r15):
What the hell happened here?   G+1024 ANA_REGS     pointer to 68 qwords: the register names packed into numbers (anaPack), by register number
What the hell happened here?   G+1032 ANA_ESCAPES  pointer to 10 qwords: the escape sequences packed into numbers, in ESCAPE_SEQUENCES order
What the hell happened here?   G+1040 ANA_ESCVALS  pointer to 10 qwords: the byte values of the escape sequences
What the hell happened here?   G+1048 ANA_TYPES    pointer to 49 qwords, by opcode: t0 + 512 * t1 + 262144 * t2 + 134217728 * pointer mask
What the hell happened here?                       (t0..t2 = the allowed PARAM_* types of the parameters, 0 = unused parameter;
What the hell happened here?                       pointer mask bit 0/1 = parameter 0/1 may be a pointer, see pointer_use in commands.rs)
What the hell happened here?   G+1056 ANA_CHILD    anaCheckCompanions: the opcode of the companion command
What the hell happened here?   G+1064 ANA_NPARAMS  anaCheckCompanions: how many parameters need a companion
What the hell happened here?   G+1072 ANA_EDITION  anaCheckCompanions: 1 for comparisons with an edition
What the hell happened here?   G+1080 ANA_END      CMDS + CMD_COUNT * 256, the end of the command records
What the hell happened here? The tables live on the stack of analyseProgram: they exist exactly as long as the analysis runs.
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Internal convention: anaParseDecimal returns a second result in rdx. Everything else is DESIGN.md.
