What the hell happened here? anaClassify(rdi = parameter, rsi = allowed types) - classify: sets TYPE and VALUE (and VERBATIM, ESCAPE for
What the hell happened here? characters) of the parameter as the first allowed type it matches, in the order register, decimal number,
What the hell happened here? character, monke label, function name, comparison label. Fails if it matches none or is too large.
What the hell happened here? r12 = parameter, r13 = allowed types, rbx = text, rbp = length
What the hell happened here? Monke labels: uauaaau|aaaa = decimal?, aaau = character?, aaua = monke?, aauu = function?, auaa = comparison label?,
What the hell happened here?               auau = fail, auua = return
